Lab 14: StatefulSet with Headless Service

1. Headless Service ivolvedbsvc

ivolvedbsvc.yaml:

yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: ivolvedbsvc
  namespace: ivolve
spec:
  clusterIP: None                 # headless
  selector:
    app: ivolvedb
  ports:
    - name: mysql
      port: 3306
      targetPort: 3306
bash
kubectl apply -f ivolvedbsvc.yaml
2. Storage for MySQL data

The StatefulSet creates its own PVC from a template. On a kubeadm cluster there is no dynamic provisioner, so you need a PV for it to bind to. The Lab 13 PV (ivolvepv) is already bound to ivolvepvc (a PV binds to one claim only), so create a second PV for the database:

bash
# on worker1
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/mysql-data

ivolvedb-pv.yaml:

yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolume
metadata:
  name: ivolvedb-pv
  labels:
    app: ivolvedb
spec:
  capacity:
    storage: 1Gi
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  persistentVolumeReclaimPolicy: Retain
  storageClassName: ""
  hostPath:
    path: /mnt/mysql-data
    type: DirectoryOrCreate
bash
kubectl apply -f ivolvedb-pv.yaml


3. StatefulSet ivolvedb

The MySQL image reads MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD, MYSQL_USER, MYSQL_PASSWORD and MYSQL_DATABASE. The ConfigMap/Secret keys from Lab 12 are DB_USER and DB_PASSWORD, which MySQL does not understand by themselves, so they are mapped to the right names below. MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD already matches, so it is read straight from the Secret.

ivolvedb.yaml:

yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: StatefulSet
metadata:
  name: ivolvedb
  namespace: ivolve
spec:
  serviceName: ivolvedbsvc        # the headless Service
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: ivolvedb
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: ivolvedb
    spec:
      nodeSelector:
        project: ivolve
      tolerations:
        - key: "workload"
          operator: "Equal"
          value: "ivolveApp"
          effect: "NoSchedule"
      containers:
        - name: mysql
          image: mysql:8.0
          ports:
            - containerPort: 3306
              name: mysql
          env:
            - name: MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD
              valueFrom:
                secretKeyRef:
                  name: ivolvesecret
                  key: MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD
            - name: MYSQL_USER
              valueFrom:
                configMapKeyRef:
                  name: ivolvecm
                  key: DB_USER
            - name: MYSQL_PASSWORD
              valueFrom:
                secretKeyRef:
                  name: ivolvesecret
                  key: DB_PASSWORD
            - name: MYSQL_DATABASE
              value: ivolve
          volumeMounts:
            - name: data
              mountPath: /var/lib/mysql
  volumeClaimTemplates:
    - metadata:
        name: data
      spec:
        accessModes: ["ReadWriteOnce"]
        storageClassName: ""
        selector:
          matchLabels:
            app: ivolvedb
        resources:
          requests:
            storage: 1Gi
bash
kubectl apply -f ivolvedb.yaml
kubectl get pods -n ivolve -w

Wait until ivolvedb-0 is 1/1 Running (MySQL can take 30-60 seconds to initialize).

4. Verify the StatefulSet and storage
bash
kubectl get statefulset,pods,svc,pvc -n ivolve -o wide
# ivolvedb-0 should be on worker1
# PVC data-ivolvedb-0 should be Bound to ivolvedb-pv

kubectl describe pod ivolvedb-0 -n ivolve | grep -iE "node:|tolerations|node-selectors"
kubectl logs ivolvedb-0 -n ivolve | tail
5. Confirm the database is operational (MySQL client)
bash
kubectl exec -it ivolvedb-0 -n ivolve -- mysql -uroot -p

Inside MySQL:

sql
SHOW DATABASES;          -- ivolve must be listed
SELECT User, Host FROM mysql.user;   -- the DB_USER user must be listed
EXIT;

Test the application user too:

bash
kubectl exec -it ivolvedb-0 -n ivolve -- mysql -u<DB_USER> -p ivolve   

6. Verify DNS resolution inside the cluster

The worker is tainted, and the control plane has its own taint, so a test pod needs the toleration to be scheduled. Use a small pod (this stays within the 3-pod quota):

dns-test.yaml:

yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: dns-test
  namespace: ivolve
spec:
  nodeSelector:
    project: ivolve
  tolerations:
    - key: "workload"
      operator: "Equal"
      value: "ivolveApp"
      effect: "NoSchedule"
  containers:
    - name: busybox
      image: busybox:1.28
      command: ["sleep", "3600"]
bash
kubectl apply -f dns-test.yaml
kubectl exec -it dns-test -n ivolve -- nslookup ivolvedbsvc
